---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import Stitch from "../components/Stitch.astro";

// TODO(Action Network): every rung below uses a mailto: fallback because the
// organization's Action Network account doesn't exist yet. Once it does
// (signup form, petition, state-legislator letter campaign — see README's
// Action Network compliance checklist), swap the marked hrefs for the
// AN-hosted pages with a ?source=<rung> code, and enable the AN widget
// embed here per the plan. Until then, every link on this page must still
// work — a mailto: link that opens the visitor's own email app does.
const email = "join@automate-ethically.com";
---

<Page
	title="Take action — Automate Ethically"
	description="Pick the step you can reach today — thirty seconds or an hour, every bit of it counts."
	ogImage="/og/act.png"
>
	<section class="ae-hero" aria-labelledby="act-title">
		<p class="ae-eyebrow">Take action</p>
		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 12: /act framing -->
		<h1 id="act-title">Pick the step you can reach today.</h1>
		<p class="ae-hero-sub">
			Rules change when neighbors organize. You don't have to do all six of
			these — even one moves the needle, and none of them cost money or ask
			you to be an expert.
		</p>
	</section>

	<Stitch />

	<section class="ae-section" aria-label="Ways to help">
		<div class="ae-container">
			<p class="ae-note">
				New here? Start with rung 1 — it takes thirty seconds, and you can
				always come back for the rest.
			</p>
			<ol class="ae-ladder">
				<li class="ae-rung" id="join">
					<span class="ae-rung-time">30 seconds</span>
					<h2 class="ae-h2">1. Join the list</h2>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 13: rung one-liners -->
					<p class="ae-prose">
						We'll email you when there's something happening in your state —
						nothing more often than that, and never anything asking for money.
					</p>
					<div class="ae-cta-row">
						<a
							class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary"
							href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Add me to the list")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("My city/town: \nMy state: \n")}`}
						>Join by email</a>
					</div>
				</li>

				<li class="ae-rung" id="petition">
					<span class="ae-rung-time">2 minutes</span>
					<h2 class="ae-h2">2. Sign the petition</h2>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 14: petition text -->
					<p class="ae-prose">
						"One rule: a human makes the decision, and answers for it."
						Signatures get shown to city councils as proof that people in
						their town care about this — not sent to any candidate or party.
					</p>
					<div class="ae-cta-row">
						<a
							class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary"
							href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Count me in on the petition")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("Name: \nCity/town: \nI support the rule: a human makes the decision, and answers for it.\n")}`}
						>Sign by email</a>
					</div>
				</li>

				<li class="ae-rung" id="share">
					<span class="ae-rung-time">5 minutes</span>
					<h2 class="ae-h2">3. Share it</h2>
					<p class="ae-prose">
						A broadside was made to be nailed up. Print
						<a href="/toolkit/one-pager">the one-pager</a> and pin it somewhere
						people will actually read it — a corkboard, a laundromat, a
						library. Or just send this page to one neighbor.
					</p>
					<div class="ae-cta-row">
						<a
							class="ae-btn ae-btn--ghost"
							href={`mailto:?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Thought you'd want to see this")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("https://automate-ethically.com")}`}
						>Email one neighbor</a>
						<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--ghost" href="/toolkit/one-pager">Print it</a>
					</div>
				</li>

				<li class="ae-rung" id="write">
					<span class="ae-rung-time">10 to 20 minutes</span>
					<h2 class="ae-h2">4. Write to your officials</h2>
					<p class="ae-prose">
						This one's really two smaller tasks, honestly costed:
					</p>
					<h3 class="ae-rung-sub">Your state representative — about 10 minutes</h3>
					<p class="ae-prose">
						They're easy to reach: look up their contact page, then copy the
						note below (in your own words is even better) and paste it in.
					</p>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 15b: this template still reads like a
					     policy memo, not a neighbor's letter. Kai's open dissent
					     (docs/adversarial-review/reviews/2026-08-29-action-ladder-accessibility.md):
					     match the plain, first-person register the rest of the toolkit uses. -->
					<blockquote class="ae-epigraph">
						<p>
							I'm a neighbor in [your town]. I'm asking you to support a rule:
							when an automated system — a camera network, an algorithm — makes
							a decision that affects someone's life, a named person has to
							review it and be accountable for it. Montana already passed this
							for state agencies (HB 178). I'd like to see it here too. Thank
							you for reading this.
						</p>
					</blockquote>
					<h3 class="ae-rung-sub">Your city council — 15 to 20 minutes, longer the first time</h3>
					<p class="ae-prose">
						We can't look up your city council for you — you know your town
						better than we do. This part takes longer because you'll need to
						find their contact info yourself.
					</p>
					<div class="ae-cta-row">
						<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--ghost" href="/toolkit/find-your-council">Find your council</a>
					</div>
				</li>

				<li class="ae-rung" id="speak">
					<span class="ae-rung-time">1 hour</span>
					<h2 class="ae-h2">5. Show up and speak</h2>
					<p class="ae-prose">
						This is the one that actually moves an ordinance. Most council
						meetings pass with almost nobody in the room — a handful of
						neighbors speaking on the same issue stands out.
					</p>
					<div class="ae-cta-row">
						<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary" href="/toolkit/council-script">Get the 2-minute script</a>
						<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--ghost" href="/toolkit/find-your-council">Find your meeting</a>
					</div>
				</li>

				<li class="ae-rung" id="lead">
					<span class="ae-rung-time">ongoing</span>
					<h2 class="ae-h2">6. Become a local lead</h2>
					<p class="ae-prose">
						<span class="ae-project-human">
							If you're willing to be the person your town calls on this — to
							host a meeting, track the council's agenda, or just be a
							point of contact — tell us what's happening where you live.
						</span>
					</p>
					<div class="ae-cta-row">
						<a
							class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary"
							href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("I want to help organize locally")}&body=${encodeURIComponent("My city/town: \nWhat's happening there: \nWhat I can help with (host a meeting / track the agenda / speak / something else): \n")}`}
						>Tell us about your town</a>
					</div>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>
</Page>
